    {
      "order": 2,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0108",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-01845-s008",
      "sentenceText": "Some people are traumatized for a long time; others decide to end their lives after a natural disaster.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7f7161f96fd223c86f67a7026558f9fac5abd1810765e53b1807455e691d6281",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-01845-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-059",
      "parentFingerprint": "f6b0ee667fd821d449243fd8195ca911eb9abb730bdf79283af8e1abbb90db58",
      "passageSha256": "ac938c1bda75d343433b1dca6756896af17bd2d1c90d991e75b269efc6f1b1ee",
      "pdfPages": [
        131
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 3,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0109",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-s001",
      "sentenceText": "However, research shows that most people are remarkably resilient.",
      "sentenceSha256": "7366562a46ce557ed4f8a9de860479479bb25bb82c6ffbe102d6ed6c7ad1beea",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-060",
      "parentFingerprint": "f5cbd2d5fabc829f4f36d70c90a94a876fc206dc67ed12d05a50bf4acf463e39",
      "passageSha256": "2fb818bcebcc392ced94343fd5c198628af4144064a4f3e4cbfed1ff516a72d5",
      "pdfPages": [
        131
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 4,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0110",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Most people do move on.",
      "sentenceSha256": "06146f05d3d0a2e8fbf8f0bcf0355a01353c0bfb24622fffb516b938f3234cbd",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-060",
      "parentFingerprint": "f5cbd2d5fabc829f4f36d70c90a94a876fc206dc67ed12d05a50bf4acf463e39",
      "passageSha256": "2fb818bcebcc392ced94343fd5c198628af4144064a4f3e4cbfed1ff516a72d5",
      "pdfPages": [
        131
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 5,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0111",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-s004",
      "sentenceText": "The idea of resilient children as remarkable individuals possessing extraordinary strength or inner resilience has lingered, even in scholarly work….",
      "sentenceSha256": "825e581fbdac23a88f1438501b2f0b759b43d7425b0e03054f7f5a836563d559",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-060",
      "parentFingerprint": "f5cbd2d5fabc829f4f36d70c90a94a876fc206dc67ed12d05a50bf4acf463e39",
      "passageSha256": "2fb818bcebcc392ced94343fd5c198628af4144064a4f3e4cbfed1ff516a72d5",
      "pdfPages": [
        131
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 6,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0112",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-s005",
      "sentenceText": "The great surprise of resilience research is the ordinariness of the phenomena.",
      "sentenceSha256": "11f6b89220e5d51c960ab56a9f09c11b5df3bd2c1ae078426b2fa3c5754d1c01",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-03795-r005-007",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-061",
      "parentFingerprint": "84e01ba1ee5561efa8b3856e5aea3d33368ee966baec32b3ec8fefb186fd8f35",
      "passageSha256": "b3705e52d760fe9f7f65bdb2132b0411b6e39f24a76a78b3d90ef17caedb6ccf",
      "pdfPages": [
        131
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 7,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0113",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-s001",
      "sentenceText": "During hard times, when happiness feels out of reach, there are other values with which we can frame our lives.",
      "sentenceSha256": "d2562f65c75c8b82949e42f54ec66505b8304754c7dcbfc57ef8481571d96b60",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-063",
      "parentFingerprint": "3e1e6524b6fe8738b8ff1919395da9a830355c40f82bdbcc373aee566b0e9099",
      "passageSha256": "d72b6494c14fd813f7c91121467cb31c31b8ce8244366ac72eeb781f411f069e",
      "pdfPages": [
        131,
        132
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 8,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0114",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-s003",
      "sentenceText": "A painting by Guido Reni shows St. Michael putting his foot on Satan’s neck.",
      "sentenceSha256": "52ed0a9deb5e69c2c60d7daa59bc361d8c79faa0b97243466bfcee968d9f77f2",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-063",
      "parentFingerprint": "3e1e6524b6fe8738b8ff1919395da9a830355c40f82bdbcc373aee566b0e9099",
      "passageSha256": "d72b6494c14fd813f7c91121467cb31c31b8ce8244366ac72eeb781f411f069e",
      "pdfPages": [
        131,
        132
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 9,
      "questionId": "qe-c11-0115",
      "sentenceId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-s004",
      "sentenceText": "William James commented on this painting, saying that “the world is all the richer for having a devil in it, so long as we keep our foot upon his neck.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "984dd639dd2f301af103b3a407b1ab1b0179ecddf28f11a474d898ea9e293e42",
      "readingUnitId": "c11-s07-p131-06330-r004-005",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c11-064",
      "parentFingerprint": "dad125e258928d9737c380cbe652fed14fe8a57a0ec5e3c66824a2d53248786f",
      "passageSha256": "7753eed9fa1d630564668d290a054ba2b55d0909401cc0edb4c88d754676ebbc",
      "pdfPages": [
        132
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0001",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In the previous chapter, I showed how the experience of a natural disaster tends to make victims become more concerned about the welfare of others and gives them a new perspective on life.",
      "sentenceSha256": "259295fcb9ba7a337eaaec7e760c2277a522935cda7382f432c38a55498583e9",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-001",
      "parentFingerprint": "115eaa7a270096c70a5f076578b762925e8459a2a81386133f33ab9f4cf28de9",
      "passageSha256": "adb55a565b406de2750b346c4b78b5b817ef49f87d261dac7ff35e24be8d6b26",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0002",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-s002",
      "sentenceText": "However, whether their experiences truly enrich their lives or not depends on the story people tell themselves.",
      "sentenceSha256": "eda76364cc036da91c8a16902b8835b00f79cdff7741abc82c601ad4e374bb8b",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-001",
      "parentFingerprint": "115eaa7a270096c70a5f076578b762925e8459a2a81386133f33ab9f4cf28de9",
      "passageSha256": "adb55a565b406de2750b346c4b78b5b817ef49f87d261dac7ff35e24be8d6b26",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0003",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-s003",
      "sentenceText": "Some stories are dramatic, memorable, and ultimately uplifting, while others are hopeless, depressing, and dark.",
      "sentenceSha256": "762f52bfbc36909ba6942f853ecfab2645db53b05a174e1ca9e9ff504e738964",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-04042-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-001",
      "parentFingerprint": "115eaa7a270096c70a5f076578b762925e8459a2a81386133f33ab9f4cf28de9",
      "passageSha256": "adb55a565b406de2750b346c4b78b5b817ef49f87d261dac7ff35e24be8d6b26",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0004",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s001",
      "sentenceText": "Psychological richness is inherently intertwined with the quantity and quality of your stories.",
      "sentenceSha256": "950e0724ee053c103aa4b55355bf2507596e551f6caa30df19ba6ceb8d717e94",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-002",
      "parentFingerprint": "c06d6f78742505e887e5c10c24b619957173884b25ef4af5cf534e13361b2fbd",
      "passageSha256": "45b41cd203e93664654e7c0a54aa02ca236bb216029265905740af1ad1dcab84",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0005",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s002",
      "sentenceText": "The more interesting stories you have, the more psychologically rich your life is.",
      "sentenceSha256": "2fb921ccdec8760d5b9116f8ce12349920ae88c311c762595a35bfb15f6c6a15",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-002",
      "parentFingerprint": "c06d6f78742505e887e5c10c24b619957173884b25ef4af5cf534e13361b2fbd",
      "passageSha256": "45b41cd203e93664654e7c0a54aa02ca236bb216029265905740af1ad1dcab84",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 15,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0006",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s004",
      "sentenceText": "How do you tell your life story?",
      "sentenceSha256": "3354db6001ee81ff7f8c4bec7907890bffc6cec4e128a411152a96109df3a070",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-002",
      "parentFingerprint": "c06d6f78742505e887e5c10c24b619957173884b25ef4af5cf534e13361b2fbd",
      "passageSha256": "45b41cd203e93664654e7c0a54aa02ca236bb216029265905740af1ad1dcab84",
      "pdfPages": [
        133
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 16,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0007",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s005",
      "sentenceText": "More generally, how much do storytelling abilities matter in creating psychological richness?",
      "sentenceSha256": "f870281cea51ba907b9f3a5766b6d4996345b2c3063db768d0d306dacc387449",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-003",
      "parentFingerprint": "0927f8f1172395b277ce2edbed2d9aa3b8bafc7741fcd06525a6aff3d0f6cb37",
      "passageSha256": "38e0993f0841f76858a54b68c8d228482d5c989d0abb14f361c83adc7c8576a2",
      "pdfPages": [
        133,
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 17,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0008",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s006",
      "sentenceText": "How much does the structure of a story matter?",
      "sentenceSha256": "1191a6eba033b2f522e27aa239be954c7fb3fffd4a7ffcbacceff10bb39a02df",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r005-008",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-003",
      "parentFingerprint": "0927f8f1172395b277ce2edbed2d9aa3b8bafc7741fcd06525a6aff3d0f6cb37",
      "passageSha256": "38e0993f0841f76858a54b68c8d228482d5c989d0abb14f361c83adc7c8576a2",
      "pdfPages": [
        133,
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 18,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0009",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-s010",
      "sentenceText": "My question to you is this: Can we make a life sound like a psychologically richer one?",
      "sentenceSha256": "c40f022136f4c38fe167cbd0622e10d4d0bc447afc2072f811a02ca60c5a3977",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s01-p133-05408-r009-010",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-004",
      "parentFingerprint": "af5290736e57c8d7fe15de9740b5a72a4f737ff0b41656187b648ed2e9e14474",
      "passageSha256": "988f5c1654b13f43c9eccf6dce59a87017517e999058d5dcb78f89cb05286aa9",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 19,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0010",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In his book Redirect, the renowned psychologist Tim Wilson discusses this exact process, which he calls “story editing.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "2c6ae93c0d32f475800a070d9a3b17884a7c2fc548487b1c2e9287d648f0f809",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-005",
      "parentFingerprint": "1a4d3296fe139b78d835cba41bc6b8069d2606d5625880041219c45d11a77e74",
      "passageSha256": "d9ab81ba4d13c9b8c1790ed89c5bef2afdd68693404f439432b40abe0acd407c",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 20,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0011",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-s003",
      "sentenceText": "For instance, one way you could edit your story would be to highlight all the challenges you faced in your life.",
      "sentenceSha256": "04747a8f1fdaddf016570d00664460e6284c5e185b0fa05fccec0475e7fb947b",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-r001-003",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-005",
      "parentFingerprint": "1a4d3296fe139b78d835cba41bc6b8069d2606d5625880041219c45d11a77e74",
      "passageSha256": "d9ab81ba4d13c9b8c1790ed89c5bef2afdd68693404f439432b40abe0acd407c",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 21,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0012",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-s004",
      "sentenceText": "G.W., who probably did not face tough challenges at Yale as a multigenerational Yalie, could say that Yale was going through a time of grave change during his college years (1964– 1968)—as antiestablishment feelings grew, legacy students like him were despised for the first time.",
      "sentenceSha256": "5c17faca6700ee5d022fb2568b447d9d738dbc457bd27a911aec773c9d92b4ac",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-r004-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-006",
      "parentFingerprint": "62192db63e6476e61a80583f995a2344a830691ad77cf2084b465ac21d661f86",
      "passageSha256": "d12a6feb87bd6779138a90d1796447bc8b08ff1ce5e7ed9467ca888c82e461d5",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 22,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0013",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-s005",
      "sentenceText": "He had to prove his own worthiness and did so in a counterproductive way, by drinking and partying too much.",
      "sentenceSha256": "f7cf7a508eb0750bfa111cc3c63ee700ea2fa347700978f00119eb9092af98c0",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p134-02235-r004-006",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-006",
      "parentFingerprint": "62192db63e6476e61a80583f995a2344a830691ad77cf2084b465ac21d661f86",
      "passageSha256": "d12a6feb87bd6779138a90d1796447bc8b08ff1ce5e7ed9467ca888c82e461d5",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 23,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0014",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p134-04770-s001",
      "sentenceText": "This is quite a healthy way of thinking about yourself.",
      "sentenceSha256": "dc9dee5300d390b8176fd2be395fef8899f7166ee18b1281bd3b2d57d259fe39",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p134-04770-r001-002",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-008",
      "parentFingerprint": "a8b46dd5482d838251285a6bd19ac0a5046f34a1e0cb62c835680b4fd2960303",
      "passageSha256": "591751a7284aaa46b48ffe0aaef33def66269fc6fdde25bc024fa4ecc4baf82e",
      "pdfPages": [
        134
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 24,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0015",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p135-02700-s001",
      "sentenceText": "However, the parents in the study might have indeed been less socially skilled and lacking self-confidence when they were young.",
      "sentenceSha256": "a3065e858fc7879fe9ddc0831fb8610460a549e7240689b7a326ca85fc85ce84",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p135-02700-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c12-012",
      "parentFingerprint": "3d9920bb144a8c0447efbb5d94bcc973dea931d2f6bf8dfdef64b59b7e5b8a23",
      "passageSha256": "82201dcfbaebaa245419f7b84ef482e77a95d2cfcc086eca4cb9ddb67e3793ab",
      "pdfPages": [
        135
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 25,
      "questionId": "qe-c12-0016",
      "sentenceId": "c12-s02-p135-02700-s004",
      "sentenceText": "At the beginning of the school year in September, they asked undergraduate participants to evaluate how independent, self-confident, and socially skilled they currently were, relative to their same-age peers in college.",
      "sentenceSha256": "c241f80661b2b6f47650fc00689ac0d8a3b412281f53a273c5ccc5586111705d",
      "readingUnitId": "c12-s02-p135-02700-r001-004",
